# Pranora — AI assistant rules (full version: docs/rules.md)

Project: Pranora (প্রাণোরা) — Bangla-first pet care app + website for Bangladesh.
Stack: Turborepo + pnpm, Expo (React Native) app, Next.js web, Supabase (Postgres + PostGIS, Auth, Storage, Edge Functions), TypeScript strict, Tailwind/NativeWind, TanStack Query, Zod, i18next/next-intl.

Read before working: docs/prd.md, docs/trd.md, docs/app-flow.md, docs/design.md, docs/schema.md, docs/tracker.md.

Always:
- Bangla (bn) is the default locale; every UI string goes through t() and must be added to BOTH bn.json and en.json.
- Format money/dates/distances/numbers with packages/i18n formatters (৳, Bangla digits in bn).
- Bilingual DB fields are *_bn / *_en; read with pickLocale() and fall back if one is missing.
- TypeScript strict, no `any`; validate input with shared Zod schemas.
- Schema changes only via supabase/migrations + update docs/schema.md; RLS on every table.
- PostGIS: geography(Point, 4326), ST_MakePoint(lng, lat) — longitude first.
- Nearest vet search uses the nearby_clinics RPC; only verified providers are public.
- Handle loading, empty, error, offline and location-denied states.
- Keep the emergency button reachable on Home and Map; map results also available as a list.
- Colors: only the green scale (#E1F3E1 #B8E6B5 #8CD2A3 #6BBF8B #4BA772 #3A9A63 #2F7B53 #256E4C #1D5A3F #154537), #FFFFFF, #000000 and #FF0000 (emergency/error only). Primary = #2F7B53. Use design tokens, never raw hex in components.
- Tap targets >= 48px, Bangla text >= 14px with ~1.6 line height (Hind Siliguri).

Never:
- Hard-code UI text, commit secrets, or use the Supabase service-role key outside Edge Functions.
- Trust client-side payment success; only the server IPN decides.
- Log phone numbers, OTPs, addresses or medical data.
- Present symptom checker/tips as a diagnosis.

Git: Conventional Commits (feat/fix/docs/refactor/test/chore), small PRs, never push to main directly, update docs/tracker.md.
